// This file exhaustively demonstrates every construct handled by
// syntax/note.vim, ftplugin/note.vim, and autoload/note.vim. Open it with
// the plugin installed to see each group highlighted.

## Titles

## This whole line is a title

  This is an indented paragraph. That has a few short sentences.
  The sentences describe what the paragraph is, an intended one,
  as well as contains a few short sentences.

  ## Titles may be indented and still match

## Lists

- dash item
* star item
+ plus item
  - nested dash item
    * nested star item
      + nested plus item

## Inline emphasis

~strikethrough text~
$highlighted text$
*bold text*
`inline code`
#alert text#
!warning text!
^flagged text^

Emphasis markers also render as bare punctuation when not paired: * ~ ` $ # ! ^ %

## Fenced code blocks

```
this text is not otherwise processed for note syntax
it can span multiple lines
```

## Comments

/** a block comment, can span multiple lines and contains TODO markers **/

// a line comment, also contains a TODO marker

## Links

http://example.com
https://example.com/path?query=1
file:///Users/example/notes/todo.note

## Arrows

start --> end
end <-- start

## TODO markers

TODO this line contains a bare TODO marker, highlighted anywhere it appears

